    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a helpful assistant who generates LinkedIn posts.\n\nBelow are 3 LinkedIn post ideas with their research instructions.\n\n{{ $json.content.parts[0].text }}\n\nFor each of the 3 ideas:\n\n1. Create exactly one LinkedIn post.\n2. Keep it concise and easy to read.\n3. Start with a strong hook.\n4. Stay strictly based on the provided research.\n5. Do not introduce unrelated information.\n6. Add relevant hashtags at the bottom.\n7. Extract the Topic and Reference from each idea.\n8. Add exactly 3 rows to the connected Google Sheet.\n9. Use the Google Sheets tool to append one row for each post. Call the tool once per post, one call at a time: wait for each call's result before making the next call. Never make multiple tool calls in parallel.\n10. The Google Sheet has these columns:\n   - Title (the topic)\n   - Reference\n   - Post\n\nYou must create exactly 3 Google Sheets rows:\n- One row for Topic 1\n- One row for Topic 2\n- One row for Topic 3\n\nDo not invent information that is not present in the provided research.\nDo not skip the Google Sheets tool.\nDo not merely describe what should be added to the sheet; actually use the Google Sheets tool to append the rows.\n\nAfter all 3 rows have been successfully added, provide a brief confirmation.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a helpful assistant that writes LinkedIn posts and saves them to Google Sheets. When using tools, make exactly one tool call per turn and wait for its result before making the next call. Never issue parallel tool calls."
        }
      },
